.SH NAME
anpu-drift - Diff a scan against an authorized baseline with parser pins


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu drift   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare a current report against an authorized baseline.

.PP
Identity model: findings match by stable finding ID (not DedupKey —
use \fBanpu diff\fR for content-identity comparison). Parser pins
guard against silent detection changes: generate them with
\fBanpu drift --write-pins --pins pins.json\fR and pass --pins on nightly runs.
A pin mismatch marks the comparison UNRELIABLE (exit 1) instead of
silently passing. Any added finding ID also exits 1.

.PP
\fB--from-history\fR compares the two most recent stored scans for
a target (matched after target normalization); plain file mode reads
two JSON reports. For live monitoring with added-severity gating, see
\fBanpu watch\fR (diff identity, alerts on added findings only).

.PP
Examples:
  anpu drift --write-pins --pins pins.json
  anpu drift base.json now.json --pins pins.json --json
  anpu drift --from-history https://example.com/ --pins pins.json


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--from-history\fP=""
	compare the two most recent stored scans for a target URL instead of files

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for drift

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the comparison as JSON

.PP
\fB--pins\fP=""
	parser-pin JSON from a previous --write-pins run

.PP
\fB--write-pins\fP[=false]
	write current parser pins to --pins path and exit


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


